# SRG-APP-000292-AU-000420  -  CAT III
# For devices and hosts within its scope of coverage, the Central Log Server
# must be configured to notify the system administrator (SA) and information
# system security officer (ISSO) when account modification events are
# received.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000292-AU-000420
group:           V-206484
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000015
control_rev5:    AC-2

contribution:    For account modification records arriving from the devices and hosts it
                 collects from, Splunk is the component that detects and notifies: a
                 scheduled saved search over those records with the email alert action
                 enabled and addressed to the system administrators and the ISSO, supported
                 by the SMTP settings in alert_actions.conf [email], is the reporting and
                 notification mechanism the product STIG fix text names.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver not_equals localhost
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search name>] enableSched equals 1
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search name>] cron_schedule non_empty
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search name>] action.email in 1|true
check:           savedsearches.conf [<search name>] action.email.to non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver non_empty -> alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver not_equals localhost
vendor:          alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/alert_actions.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The requirement is not applicable where notifications are performed by
                 another device, which the check text states explicitly; that determination
                 is made from the system architecture, not from Splunk configuration.
external:        Coverage depends on the devices and hosts in scope actually sending their
                 account modification records to Splunk, which rests on those endpoints'
                 own logging configuration and on the collection path to the indexers.
external:        The SMTP relay is external to the product by the specification's own
                 statement, and the recipient addresses and reporting frequency are
                 organization-defined.
external:        The product STIG establishes this by interviewing the administrator and
                 the ISSO, so receipt of the report is confirmed procedurally.
external:        Whether the saved search's query selects account modification records from
                 the sources in scope is search language content for a reviewer to inspect,
                 not a configuration value.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/alert_actions.conf.spec:157-161 ([email]), 276-285
                 (mailserver, SMTP server not included with the instance);
                 splunk-spec-files/savedsearches.conf.spec:73-78 (enableSched = [0 | 1],
                 default 0), 79-90 (cron_schedule), 270-274 (alert_condition), 300-303
                 (action.email, default false), 304-307 (action.email.to, REQUIRED);
                 SRG-APP-000292-AU-000420 check text, including its not-applicable clause
                 where notifications are performed by another device; product STIG
                 SPLK-CL-000020 check and fix text.
finding:         Splunk is not configured to notify the SA and the ISSO when account
                 modification events are received from the devices and hosts in its scope
                 of coverage, because no scheduled saved search with the email action
                 enabled and addressed to those recipients exists, or alert_actions.conf
                 [email] names no SMTP relay; this is assessed at the application layer
                 alone, and where another device performs these notifications the
                 requirement is not applicable, with the mail relay, the sources' own
                 logging, the recipient addresses, and confirmation of receipt recorded as
                 external dependencies.
